# Docs travel with the change

A requested change is not done until matching documentation is updated in the **same turn**. Do not leave docs for a later agent, commit, or chat.

## When to update

Update docs when the change alters any of: user flow, UI copy, API routes, env vars, scripts, project layout, auth, OAuth setup, or package public API.

Skip when the change is comments-only, tests-only, or an internal refactor with the same public contract.

## Where to write

Edit the existing file that already documents that surface. Keep one source of truth; do not duplicate the same paragraph across files.

| Surface | File |
| --- | --- |
| What the app does, setup, env table, API routes, scripts | `README.md` |
| Stack, layout, flows, internals | `docs/implementation.md` |
| Better Auth, SQLite, other databases | `docs/better-auth.md` |
| Creating OAuth apps and filling `.env.local` | `docs/oauth-setup.md` |
| `@github-connector/auth` install and API | `packages/auth/README.md` |

Add a new doc only when the change introduces a surface none of these cover, and link it from `README.md`.

## How to update

1. Diff the change against the table above.
2. Patch every matching file so a reader of that file alone would not be misled.
3. Drop or rewrite stale names, routes, env vars, and steps the change retired.

Done when every contract change has a matching doc edit, or you have confirmed no documented surface moved.

```
# ✅ GOOD — new env var lands in code and README in the same turn
AUTH_DATABASE_PATH added to lib/auth.js
AUTH_DATABASE_PATH row added to README.md and docs/implementation.md

# ❌ BAD — ship the code and mention docs later
AUTH_DATABASE_PATH added to lib/auth.js
"we should update the README next"
```
